{
	// The repo's own Node tooling: the CI guard scripts under `scripts/` and
	// `apps/backend/scripts/`, the composite action's test under `.github/`,
	// and the placeholder Lambda under `infra/`. There is no root
	// `tsconfig.json` in this repo, so until § 757 none of it was in any tsc
	// program at all — 35 files whose verdicts every merge depends on.
	//
	// `types` is explicit because nothing here pulls `@types/node` in on its
	// own: the automatic type-root scan does not fire under this config chain
	// and `moduleResolution: bundler` skips `node:`-prefixed specifiers, so
	// without it every `process` and every `node:fs` import reads as an
	// unresolved name (the same trap § 752 recorded).
	//
	// `lib` is `esnext` alone, without `DOM`. These are Node processes; a
	// `document` or a `localStorage` reaching one of them is a mistake, and
	// everything a script legitimately uses (`fetch`, `URL`, `console`) comes
	// from `@types/node`.
	//
	// Run: `npm run check:script-types`
	// CI:  the `parity-types` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
	// The include list is guarded by scripts/tsconfig_coverage.test.mjs.
	"extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
	"compilerOptions": {
		"lib": ["esnext"],
		"types": ["node"]
	},
	"include": [
		".github/**/*.mjs",
		"apps/backend/scripts/**/*.mjs",
		"infra/**/*.mjs",
		"scripts/**/*.mjs"
	]
}
